# The published design canvas: ~2.5MB of editor runtime seeded around the
# artboards. It is build output -- regenerate it from the tracked .dc.html
# files and canvas.json with the design skill's seeder rather than storing it:
#
#   node <skill>/seed-canvas.mjs --template <skill>/payload.template.html \
#     --out job-triage-ui.html --title "Job Triage UI" \
#     --artboard Main.dc.html --artboard Current.dc.html \
#     --artboard Phone.dc.html --artboard JobCard.dc.html --canvas canvas.json
job-triage-ui.html

# Throwaway copy of the app with the config script stripped, so CLOUD is false
# and it runs local-only. Used to reach the screens that sit behind the sign-in
# wall while testing. Built on demand, never edited by hand.
__preview_local.html

# Design-tool exports. The .dc.html sources and the tokens are tracked under
# design/; these are the runtime and the packaging around them.
*.zip
design/support.js
.thumbnail
Job triage app mockups/
Job triage UI color system/

# Server secrets for `supabase secrets set --env-file`. Never commit.
supabase/.env
supabase/.temp/

# Per-machine tool state -- local debug configs, session dumps -- never the
# same across two machines and never something to sync through the repo.
#
# Not .claude/ wholesale, though it was until 2026-09-18. Ignoring the whole
# directory also swallowed .claude/settings.json -- the SHARED project settings
# file, the one Claude Code's docs say to commit so teammates get it -- along
# with .claude/skills, commands and agents, which are repo-level config too. So
# nothing about how this project is worked on could be shared through the repo
# at all, which is how a plugin install came to persist nowhere. Only the
# genuinely per-machine files are named now:
#   *.local.json   settings.local.json and friends: personal overrides for this
#                  one project, which the docs say to keep out of git
#   launch.json    the local debug config this section was added for (34a2c6a)
# A machine-local file nobody thought to name here shows up as untracked in git
# status: noticeable, and harmless. Note this is the opposite shape to
# .assetsignore, which allow-lists precisely because a file it fails to name is
# served to the public. Here the worse mistake is the other one -- silently
# failing to share something that was meant to be shared -- so the rule names
# what to exclude rather than what to keep.
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/launch.json
claude --teleport*.txt

# Index build output: crawl it, do not commit it (37 MB per 5k jobs).
scripts/index/index.jsonl
scripts/index/candidates.jsonl
scripts/index/vectors.bin
scripts/index/vectors.json
scripts/index/node_modules/

# Wrangler's own local dev state, generated by `wrangler dev`/`wrangler deploy`
# run locally. Never the same across two machines; regenerated on demand.
.wrangler/
worker-configuration.d.ts
